@startuml OAC power up to S5

participant Baseboard
participant OAC 

== OAC Power on O0 to O3 ==
note left of Baseboard
O0
end note
Baseboard <- OAC: Assert OAC_PRSNT[0:6]#
note right of Baseboard
OAC_PRSNT[0:6]# assertion is initiated by physical insertion
and seating of the OAC. Presence is indicated by
grounding OAC_PRSNT[0:6]# or MPESTI-based discovery.
end note
Baseboard -> Baseboard: Check OAC Adapter Presence
note left of Baseboard
O1
end note
Baseboard -> OAC: Provide +12V Auxliary Power
OAC -> OAC: Enable standby VRs, clocks, USB-Hubs...
OAC -> OAC: Validate standby power environment
OAC -> Baseboard: Assert OAC_AUX_PWR_GD
note left of Baseboard
O2
end note
Baseboard -> OAC: Deassert OAC_MC_RST#
OAC -> OAC: Initialize MC subsystem
OAC -> OAC: Boot MC
OAC -> OAC: Enable MCTP/PLDM services
OAC -> Baseboard: OAC_MC_RDY
note left of Baseboard
O3
end note
Baseboard -> OAC: Enumerate management interface
Baseboard -> OAC: Establish MCTP/PLDM communication
Baseboard -> OAC: Query OAC connector interface definition (CID)
Baseboard -> OAC: Query OAC slot configuration data definitions (SCDD)
Baseboard -> Baseboard: Check platform compatibility against CID
Baseboard -> Baseboard: Derive slot configuration data assignments (SCDA)
Baseboard -> OAC: Write slot configuration data assignments (SCDA) to OAC
OAC -> OAC: Validate SCDA against operational requirements
OAC -> Baseboard: Accept the configuration

== OAC Power on from O3 to O5 ==
note left of Baseboard
O3
end note
Baseboard -> Baseboard: Energize primary power bus bar
Baseboard -> OAC: Assert OAC_PWR_EN
OAC -> OAC: Enable VRs, Clocks...
OAC -> Baseboard: Assert OAC_PWR_GD
note right of Baseboard
When multiple OACs are installed within a platform, 
primary power may be applied sequentially. 
As a result, the time between OAC_PWR_GD assertion 
and the next primary power-up event may vary and 
is platform-dependent.
end note
note left of Baseboard
O4
end note

Baseboard -> OAC: Deassert OAC_PLT_RST#
OAC -> OAC: Intialize devices in primary power domain
Baseboard -> OAC: Enumerate Devices
note left of Baseboard
O5
end note

== OAC Power throttling from O5 to O6 ==
note left of Baseboard
O5
end note
alt baseboard initialized
Baseboard -> OAC: Write Operational Power Limit
OAC -> OAC: Reduce Power to new limit
else adapter initialized
OAC -> OAC: Reduce Power to a new limit
end
OAC -> Baseboard: OPL PLDM Transition Event
note left of Baseboard
O6
end note
== OAC Power throttling from O5/O6 to O7 ==
note left of Baseboard
O5/O6
end note
Baseboard -> OAC: Assert PWRBRK#
OAC -> OAC: Reduce Power to OPL-EMG
OAC -> Baseboard: OPL PLDM Transition Event
note left of Baseboard
O7
end note




@enduml